    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259-a1">

                <pb facs="0429" n="335" xml:id="pg335"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 to No. 775.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Rosebery to Mr.
                            Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 22d of
                    August, in which I forwarded a copy of the animals (amendment) order of 1892,
                    No. 7, permitting sheep brought from the United States to be landed in Great
                    Britain without being subject to slaughter, I have now the honor to inclose copy
                    of a further order passed by the board of agriculture on the 14th instant, which
                    amends the condition of landing prescribed by article 3 of the first-mentioned
                    order.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. H. Sanderson.</hi><lb/>(For the Earl
                        of Rosebery.)</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
